## 4.1 DNS Zone Transfer Unrestricted

### F-01   BIND 9.11.5-P4 -- allow-transfer { any; } -- MEDIUM

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| Description | The BIND DNS server is configured with `allow-transfer { any; };`, permitting any host to request a full zone copy via AXFR. This exposed `preprod-payroll.trick.htb`, a subdomain not otherwise discoverable without active vhost fuzzing. |
| Prerequisites | Network access to TCP port 53. No credentials required. |
| Impact | Full DNS zone enumeration. Internal hostnames, subdomains and infrastructure exposed to any external party. |
| Affected system | trick.htb port 53/tcp -- ISC BIND 9.11.5-P4 |
| CVSS 3.1 | 5.3 -- AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N |
| CWE | CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information |

**Steps to reproduce:**

1. `dig -x <TARGET_IP> @<TARGET_IP>` to retrieve the domain name.
2. `dig axfr trick.htb @<TARGET_IP>` to dump the full zone.

**Evidence:**

```
$ dig axfr trick.htb @<TARGET_IP>
preprod-payroll.trick.htb. 604800 IN A <TARGET_IP>
```

**Remediation:** Set `allow-transfer { none; };` globally in the BIND options block. Permit transfers only to authorised secondary nameserver IPs per zone. Audit all DNS zones for records exposing internal infrastructure.

**Verification:** Confirm `dig axfr trick.htb @<TARGET_IP>` returns `Transfer failed` or is refused with NOTAUTH.

